# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE RULE: no generated slate data is ever committed to `main`.
#
# The repo hit 20+ GB because bot output (76 MB slate JSONs, 100 MB graded
# results, tens of thousands of per-player cache files) was being committed
# every run by several workflows. That is what made Streamlit Cloud time out
# cloning the repo -- it never got past "Cloning repository...".
#
# Data now lives on the `data` branch as a single force-pushed orphan commit
# containing only the few small files the app reads (see
# .github/scripts/publish_data.sh). main stays code-only, a few MB.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bot output and caches — regenerated every run, never source
public/data/
bots/outputs/
bots/*.sqlite
bots/*.sqlite-journal
bots/pair_history_cache.json
bots/pair_history_summary.json
outputs/
bot_outputs/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# env
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# legacy Next.js / Vercel (removed in the Streamlit migration; kept so a
# stale local build directory can't get committed by accident)
node_modules
.next/
out/
build
.vercel
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Local scratch in the push folder - never belongs in the repo (2026-08-22)
_stale_git_locks/
_to_delete/
*.bundle
*.patch
